Section II: Course Details
Detailed Description

Students analyze new and existing products and operational project analysis. They also study the concepts of investment analysis which includes investment appraisal, risk and sensitivity analysis and mutually exclusive alternative investment methods. Students investigate various aspects of entrepreneurship including market research, project financing, as well as business planning, intellectual property and filing patents. Through individual assignments, case studies, project work and an exam students demonstrate their knowledge and skills of many concepts of engineering economics.

