Course Critical Performance and Learning Outcomes

 	Critical Performance:
By the end of this course, students will have demonstrated the ability to write a business plan for engineering projects, taking into account market research, investment analysis, project financing and budgeting techniques, through the application of economic and accounting principles.
 	
Learning Outcomes:

To achieve the critical performance, students will have demonstrated the ability to:

Evaluate the economic feasibility of new products and manufacturing processes (EP.3).
Evaluate existing product offerings to determine how they are contributing to the economic viability of the business (EP.3).
Describe the role, relevance and effectiveness of investment analysis and budgeting techniques used in the management of manufacturing processes (EP.2, EP.3).
Develop replacement decisions through the application of cost benefit analysis and variance analysis (EP.3).
Identify the impact of inflation, taxation uncertainty and risk inherent in business operational and investment decisions (EP.1, EP.3).
Apply the principles of engineering economics to assess the impacts of engineering solutions (EP.3, IE.1) .
Estimate costs and perform an economic analysis in support of capstone design and other term projects (EP.2, EP.3).
Conduct market research for engineering projects (IN.1, IN.2, IN.3).
Assess patentability and intellectual property for engineering projects (LL.1).
Define the value proposition for engineering projects (EP.3).
Write a business plan for engineering projects (CS.1, CS.2).

